  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ResumeData
  applicantName: Zara Okonkwo
  body: '<b>ZARA OKONKWO</b>

    Applying for: Vice President of Everything


    <b>EXPERIENCE</b>

    {title}
    - Brightwave Industries

    {dates}

    {achievement}


    <b>EDUCATION</b>

    {edu}


    <b>SKILLS</b>

    {skill_meetings}


    <b>REFERENCES</b>

    {ref}'
  claims:
  - id: title
    text: Chief Operating Officer
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 2
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: COO is a big job. What did you actually do?
      answer: I ran daily operations for {o_people} people. I also {o_meetings}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: o_people
        text: 3,000
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Three thousand. I knew most of their names. And all of their
          birthdays.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
      - id: o_meetings
        text: cancelled every meeting that could have been an email
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: It saved the company 40,000 hours a year. Productivity doubled.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: COO experience is exactly what we need.
      answer: And I'm ready to do it again. Ideally with fewer people crying in the
        elevator.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: dates
    text: 2014 - 2026
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 1
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Why leave Brightwave after 12 years?
      answer: Competitor Corp bought them. Their first order was to {c_rename}. I
        quit that afternoon.
      demeanor: 0
      phrases:
      - id: c_rename
        text: rename every meeting room after their CEO
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: There were 40 rooms called 'Greg'. I couldn't do it.
        callOutDemeanor: 0
    goodQuestion:
      question: Twelve years shows loyalty.
      answer: I believe in finishing what I start. Even this sentence.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: achievement
    text: Grew revenue 300% in 5 years
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 0
    designerNote: Sounds too good, but she has the receipts.
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: 300% revenue growth. That sounds too good to be true.
      answer: It does! I {r_report}. Most of it came from {r_product}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: r_report
        text: brought the annual reports
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Here. Page 12. The big green arrow is me.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
      - id: r_product
        text: selling umbrellas to a very rainy country
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Very rainy. Very grateful.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: 300% growth is incredible.
      answer: Thank you. It took a lot of spreadsheets. And one very good umbrella.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: edu
    text: MBA, Westbridge School of Business
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 0
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Is your MBA from a real school?
      answer: Westbridge, class of 2010. I still have the {m_debt}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: m_debt
        text: student debt
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Just kidding. I paid it off. It took a while.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: An MBA. Solid.
      answer: I graduated top of my class. Second place still sends me angry emails.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: skill_meetings
    text: Shortening meetings
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 4
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: How do you 'shorten meetings'?
      answer: Everyone stands. No chairs. Meetings end very quickly when everyone's
        {s_legs}.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: s_legs
        text: legs get tired
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Fifteen minutes, maximum. People call it 'the Zara Rule'.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: We desperately need shorter meetings.
      answer: I noticed. Your lobby has a sign that says 'Meeting in Progress' and
        it's covered in dust.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  - id: ref
    text: Marcus Chen, former CEO of Brightwave
    isSuspicious: 0
    category: 5
    designerNote: 
    suspiciousQuestion:
      question: Will Brightwave's former CEO really vouch for you?
      answer: Marcus? He has {m_tried} to hire me back.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases:
      - id: m_tried
        text: tried three times
        isContradiction: 0
        callOutResponse: Four, actually. He sends fruit baskets. I'm not going back.
        callOutDemeanor: 1
    goodQuestion:
      question: A CEO reference is strong.
      answer: Marcus will tell you I'm stubborn. He's right. I'm stubborn about doing
        things well.
      demeanor: 1
      phrases: []
  referenceLetter: 'To whom it may concern,


